 "implementation_choices": [
  "Signal frequency f = Omega/(2 pi) computed exactly (spec prints f = 0.0159155 for a = b = 1 and 0.063662 for the canonical frame); the projection frequency is Omega = 2 pi f.",
  "Step counts: n_burn = round(10 periods / dt), n_meas = round(50 periods / dt) (62,832 and 314,159 at dt = 0.01, as the spec states; 125,664 and 628,319 at dt = 0.005; the canonical frame at dt = 0.0025 has the same step counts as a = b = 1 at dt = 0.01). T = n_meas * dt.",
  "Random numbers: run (frame, dt, D, seed) uses np.random.default_rng(seed) and draws standard normals step by step for the 400 trials (row = step). 'Same seeds' for the dt and frame checks means the same seed numbers. Because the canonical frame at dt = 0.0025 is an exact rescaling of the a = b = 1 Euler map at dt = 0.01, the frame check with the same seeds reproduces the main runs up to rounding: it tests the scaling and the code path, not an independent statistical replicate. At dt = 0.005 the increments are different draws, so the dt comparison includes seed noise.",
  "Trial k starts in the well -1 (k even) or +1 (k odd), as BistableDoubleWell.simulate().",
  "Estimator exactly as spec: c_k = (2/T) sum x(t) exp(-i Omega t) dt over the window; per seed M = mean_k c_k, s2 = sum_k |c_k - M|^2 / (n - 1); eta = (|M|^2 - s2/n) / A^2. Mean and SE (sd/sqrt(10)) over the 10 seeds.",
  "dt rule: rel_k = |eta_dt0.005(D_k) - eta_dt0.01(D_k)| / eta_dt0.01(D_k) for D_k in {0.10, 0.15, 0.30} (seed means). If any rel_k > 0.02, every gated value is taken from dt = 0.005: dt = 0.005 is run over the window D in [0.12, 0.18] and also at D = 0.20 (needed for condition 3); D = 0.30 at dt = 0.005 comes from the check itself.",
  "Frame check: 16 * eta_canonical vs eta (a = b = 1, dt = 0.01) at each check D; agreement means |diff| <= 2 * sqrt(SE1^2 + SE2^2). A failure is recorded and the gating evaluation is withheld (spec: investigate before gating).",
  "Peak: np.polyfit(D, seed-mean eta, 2) on the 7 window points; D_max = -b/(2a), eta_max = c - b^2/(4a) (a < 0 required). Bootstrap: 1000 resamples of the 10 seeds with replacement (same resample at every D), rng seed 2626; SE = sd of the bootstrap vertex values.",
  "SNR (reported only): per trial X_k(w_m) = sum x exp(-i w_m t) dt at the 10 bins w_m = 2 pi m / T, m = m0 +- 1..5 (m0 = 50, the bin of Omega); background S_N = mean over bins of sum_k |X_k - mean_k X_k|^2 / ((n - 1) T); SNR = pi * (|M|^2 - s2/n) / S_N (RMP Eq. 2.13 convention with S(w) = int e^{i w tau} <x x> d tau). Reported: grid D of local maxima of the seed-mean SNR and a 3-point quadratic vertex around the interior local maximum, against Delta V / 2 = 0.125."
 ],
